TC06 - Verify Responsive Navigation Menu on Mobile Viewport

Test Steps
Step	Action	Expected Result
1	Set the browser viewport to a mobile size (e.g., 375x667).	Viewport is resized successfully.
2	Open https://playwright.dev/	Playwright homepage is displayed in mobile layout.
3	Verify the main navigation links (Docs, API, etc.) are hidden/collapsed.	Standard nav bar is not visible; a hamburger/menu icon is shown instead.
4	Click the hamburger/menu icon.	A mobile navigation drawer/menu expands.
5	Verify the expanded menu contains the same navigation links as desktop (Docs, API, Community, etc.).	All primary nav links are visible within the mobile menu.
6	Click the "Docs" link from within the mobile menu.	The documentation page opens and the mobile menu closes.
7	Verify the page renders correctly in mobile viewport (no horizontal overflow/broken layout).	Page content fits within the mobile viewport width.

Expected Final Result
The user can successfully access and use the site's full navigation via the collapsed mobile menu, and the resulting page renders correctly on a mobile viewport.